diff --git a/qemu/docs/specs/pcie-vip.rst b/qemu/docs/specs/pcie-vip.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c60a827
--- /dev/null
+++ b/qemu/docs/specs/pcie-vip.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+QEMU PCIe VIP
+============
+
+``pcie-vip`` is a non-migratable PCIe endpoint for verification.  It has
+vendor/device ID ``1234:11e9``, class ``0xff00``, a 64 KiB BAR0 register
+window, and four MSI-X vectors in BAR2.  The device connects to an external
+Mini-ICS v2 server over a Unix socket; the external process owns the
+deterministic register model or an Alex Forencich RTL endpoint.
+
+Example::
+
+  qemu-system-x86_64 -machine q35 \
+    -device pcie-vip,socket=/tmp/pcie-vip.sock,timeout-ms=5000
+
+The socket must be accepting before QEMU realizes the device.  BAR reads and
+writes are little-endian and preserve byte enables.  Endpoint DMA is executed
+with QEMU's ``pci_dma_read``/``pci_dma_write`` APIs, so guest IOMMU mappings
+and bounds checks are honored.  A runtime disconnect makes reads return all
+ones and rejects writes/DMA; restart QEMU to reconnect.
+
+QEMU validates guest-visible PCI behavior only.  PHY, LTSSM, DLLP, and lane
+training remain out of scope and should be exercised with cocotbext-pcie.
diff --git a/qemu/hw/misc/pcie-vip.c b/qemu/hw/misc/pcie-vip.c
